When you roll Initiative, gain a Seed Die at d6 instead of a d4.
}}

{{note2,wide

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; margin-bottom:2px;"><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
Ingrain
</span><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
</span></div>

Action: Gain temp HP equal to STR×LVL. You are Restrained until the end of your next turn, and cannot be moved aginst your will. Any remaining temp HP is lost once you're no longer Restrained.
}}

{{note2,wide

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; margin-bottom:2px;"><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
Efficient Cultivation
</span><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
</span></div>

You may use Cultivate Flora twice per turn instead of once.
}}

{{note2,wide

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; margin-bottom:2px;"><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
Branching Vines
</span><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
</span></div>
When you hit with Thorn Whip, you may expend a Seed Die: deal the same damage to a second creature adjacent to your target.
}}

{{note2,wide

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; margin-bottom:2px;"><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
Bramble Lash
</span><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
</span></div>
On hit with Thorn Whip, instead of dealing damage, you may Grapple the target if they are your size or smaller. If they're larger than you, move onto them and gain the Riding condition.
}}

{{note2,wide

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; margin-bottom:2px;"><span style="font-family:beaufort-pro; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:900; font-style:italic; white-space:nowrap;">
